<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="47325" href="schedule/2007/spring/ARTS/499/47325.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2007" href="schedule/2007.xml">2007</calendarYear><term id="120071" href="schedule/2007/spring.xml">Spring 2007</term><subject id="ARTS" href="schedule/2007/spring/ARTS.xml">Art--Studio</subject><course id="499" href="schedule/2007/spring/ARTS/499.xml">Special Topics in Studio Art</course></parents><sectionNumber>AD2</sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Art and Context.  Art and Context is a studio/seminar established on the belief that the context of artistic production is just as significant as the production itself.  This course is designed to examine the histories of site-based practice and critically engage the production of space through readings, studio projects, situated interventions, and on-site critiques.  Graduate Section.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2007-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2007-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>04:00 PM</start><end>06:40 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><instructors><instructor lastName="Bakker" firstName="C">Bakker, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>